
@startuml
' PetPals - Section 4.4.1
' Representative booking lifecycle sequence diagram
' Based on UC-006, UC-007, UC-009 and database.md

title PetPals - Booking Lifecycle Sequence Diagram

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam maxMessageSize 220
hide footbox

actor "Pet Owner" as Owner
actor "Pet Helper" as Helper
participant "React PWA" as PWA
participant "Node.js API" as API
database "PostgreSQL" as DB
participant "Google Calendar API" as Calendar

== 1. Booking Request (UC-006) ==

Owner -> PWA: Select service, pet, dates and handover address
PWA -> API: Submit booking request

API -> DB: Validate user approval, pet ownership,\nlisting eligibility and availability
DB --> API: Validation result

break Invalid or unavailable request
    API --> PWA: Reject request with reason
end

API -> DB: Create booking (status=requested)
API --> PWA: Booking Requested

== 2. Helper Decision (UC-007) ==

Helper -> PWA: Review booking and choose decision
PWA -> API: Submit helper decision

break Helper declines
    API -> DB: Verify helper and Requested status;\nset booking status=declined
    API --> PWA: Booking Declined
end

API -> DB: Verify helper and atomically reserve slot;\nset booking status=accepted
DB --> API: Reservation result

break Unauthorized helper or reservation conflict
    API --> PWA: Booking not approved
end

API --> PWA: Booking Approved

note over API,DB
    Booking acceptance reserves the selected time slot.
    Overlapping reservations must be prevented.
end note

== 3. Google Calendar Synchronization ==

loop For each participant with calendar authorization
    API -> Calendar: Create event with booking details
    Calendar --> API: Event ID or error
    API -> DB: Record calendar synchronization status
end

note over API,Calendar
    Calendar failures do not cancel an accepted booking.
    Retry handling follows the agreed integration policy.
end note

== 4. Service Start Confirmation (UC-009) ==

Helper -> PWA: Initiate Start using in-app buttons
PWA -> API: Create Start confirmation attempt
API -> DB: Save pending attempt with expiry

Helper -> PWA: Confirm service start
PWA -> API: Submit helper confirmation
API -> DB: Record helper confirmation

Owner -> PWA: Confirm service start
PWA -> API: Submit owner confirmation

API -> DB: Verify both confirmations\non the same unexpired attempt

alt Both confirmations valid
    API -> DB: Mark attempt confirmed;\nset booking status=in_progress
    API --> PWA: Booking In Progress
else Incomplete or expired
    API --> PWA: Booking remains Accepted
end

note over Owner,API
    QR confirmation (UC-010) is an alternative method.
    The helper displays the QR code and the owner scans it.
    Both participants must still confirm the service start.
end note

@enduml
